  "raw": " her friend's house last July 4 and got quickly caught up in the yard birds. She loved to explore the yard but one day, a hawk swooped down and Snowball fell and hit her head on a picnic table just below their level. We were able to gently lift her up and bring her outside and an inspection found her with damage to both her head and her body. She was taken care of for a couple of weeks then was released back into the yard where she began eagerly flapping her wings and exploring the yard again. Unfortunately, while she was recovering from this, Jake learned to jump over picnic tables - something that no longer allowed her to freely explore her environment! Although we kept a close eye on her every time she was outside (and still do), after a couple of months it has become evident that no matter how much love gets poured in, Jake just can't be loved like a pet. We have yearned to introduce her to another willing family who would love to give her",
